<title>USA: Raytheon declines comment on Hughes bid.</title>
<headline>Raytheon declines comment on Hughes bid.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Raytheon Co declined to comment on reports it raised its bid for Hughes Electronics Corp to around $10 billion.</p>
<p>&quot;Our policy is not to comment on speculation on mergers and acquisitions,&quot; spokesman Robert McWade told Reuters.</p>
<p>The Boston Globe reported Friday that Raytheon and rival bidder Northrop Grumman Corp each raised their offers for the General Motors Corp unit to around $10 billion, and GM was to hold a board of directors meeting Friday to consider the bids.</p>
<p>Both companies added about $1 billion to their final bids submitted on Wednesday, persons close to the bidding told the newspaper.</p>
<p>((Boston bureau, (617) 367-4106))</p>
